00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000 align:start position:0%
 
fortnight has become so incredibly  massive and all-encompassing that people  who have never even heard of the game  have been subjected to articles and news  pieces flooding their feeds and plastic  llamas wandering their streets but in  the lead-up to fortnight season five  epic games created an Arg or alternate  reality game where the game world and  our world really did collide it kicked  off with the shared world event of  season fours rocket launch that created  tears in the game sky eventually leading  to the current worlds collide event in  season 5 there were tons of hints and  clues for inquisitive players to  discover within the game and even in the  real world so if you weren't glued to  the subreddit like me or are just  getting into fortnight now here's why  the new season was so hyped and why you  may have seen news stories about giant  burgers appearing in the desert  throughout June 2018 there were plenty  of teases that a rocket would be  launched by the visitor the skin that  was earned as a reward for completing  seven blockbuster season four challenges  can down clucksten skulls were displayed  on TVs and rocket schematics was seen in  bases but on the 29th of June epic gave  players a message getting match on  Saturday by 10:30 a.m. Pt 1:30 p.m. ET  7:30 p.m. CET and look to the sky it  only happens once  of course players swarmed into service  to see what was going on many was so  enthralled that dozens of people even  dropped their arms to stare at the stars  on viewing platforms which other players  took advantage of  as the rocket launched and traveled  through the skies of a fortnight's  island rift started appearing in the sky  culminating in one huge crack above the  map which slowly expanded over the days  following during this launch sequence  two audio files were heard in the  background  crafty players were then able to  discover data within those audio files  using a spectrogram the first audio  sequence showed the skulls that were  also present on the countdown TV screens  while the second showed two sets of  numbers that were decoded to show four  different coordinates on the map and B 6  h 9i 8 and i 9 they were originally  believed to be a hint to a new game mode  to see off season 4 but the coordinates  ended up matching up with rifts and  items appearing or disappearing like the  appearance of an anchor at B 6 and an  old-time carriage at I 8 of course now  that we can see the whole season 5 map  we know that a Viking ship in town  appears at B 6 and the last three  coordinates are now home to the new  desert biome with objects vanishing from  the map and others unexpectedly  appearing people start to pay closer  attention to the subtleties of four  nights world but perhaps the most  interesting incident actually manifested  in the real world itself on the 6th of  July the user seller Salone on Twitter  tweeted what is this I'm in the middle  of the desert why is this here with an  attached picture of the derp burger  which had previously vanished from the  forum map via one of the rift anomalies  also present in the Californian desert  was one of the fortnight police cars  [Music]  soon after that discovery agents started  appearing on sites putting up a tent  scattered with items and surrounding the  burger with caution tape once agents had  started appearing on the scene crowds  followed Reddit user boy e QQ Hugh  captured an interaction with agent 3 6 7  8 in the video you can see the agent  hand out card that card had the number 7  1 2 3 a 0 4 0 9 1 if that number was  called after the 8th of July this  admittedly not very pleasant noise would  play  [Music]  following the pattern sneaky game  detectives took from the rocket launch  audio files this sound was put under a  spectrogram to reveal a similar code  this time the numbers were decoded to  show the coordinate of c7 the location  of greasy Grove and the spot where the  derp burger vanished from the game world  the ID numbers of the agents were also  an easter-egg themselves typing each of  the numbers into a phone's keypad would  reveal the words fort night and epoch do  you know anything about season five  season five of what three days later on  the 9th of July supply llama started to  appear in seemingly random locations in  Europe one in Cologne Germany another  found in Barcelona Spain one in Warsaw  Poland two in London England and one in  Cannes France the seventh was only found  after a new sound fire was discovered  when calling the number on the agents  card dialling six after calling the  number would play a new sound and  putting that audio into a spectrogram in  the same way the previous sound files  had been treated revealed the  coordinates of the seventh llama  following those coordinates it was  finally found in Paris France although  the game detectives wiki currently lists  it as robbed /m I a so some someone  steal a llama after that we only had to  wait until the 12th of July until things  started to make sense the build-up was  to the season five worlds collide event  skins and carts and objects and  buildings were brought from our real  world and into fortnight and apparently  in exchange we got llamas and giant  burger but if there's one game that  benefits from the excitement of  colliding worlds right now it's for  night the buzz and hype around the game  is in a constant ebb and flow it's been  a long time since I've seen mainstream  media report on a game like this in such  a big way or a game be talked about in  such common parlance it's as much a  phenomenon as any media property can  rightly become but why did people get so  caught up in countdown clogs rockets and  plastic alarms and phone booths for me  at least it showcased the infectious  curiosity of the community and the  creativity that's possible in a game  like this when its developer cares and  is willing to put in the effort to  engage its audience in more interesting  ways the biggest achievement of this Arg  is to strengthen four-night as a game  that offers more than just a core  gameplay loop of loot  building and trying to be the sole  survivor when you step back and look at  it there are many games that have either  done individual elements of these or all  of them together in a similar fashion  but what this Arg does is show for  tonight as a game with a world that  people are attached to characters  cosmetics and even dances that have  become recognizable we dare say iconic  but our games are a dime a dozen right  now but none of them have people  discussing the actual world they take  place in or taking selfies with objects  that have slipped into our real world  that this one island can be full of  intrigue and mystery that there's things  to find see and discuss and that plots  and stories can be given to what in many  other games would be purely cosmetic  skins is an impressive achievement and  undoubtedly the clearest indication the  battery our games can offer much more  than the thrill of victory from what I  saw most the community loved the Arg  there were many that dismissed it as a  PR stunt which is fair enough but in  many ways that's all Arg severa  in this case it triggered discussion and  teamwork and interesting conversations  and theories within the community the  fortnight be our subreddit was an  exciting place to be during the event  and seeing people's genuine excitement  and predictions was infectious as was  seeing the video where players banded  together to create a viewing platform to  share it still fills me with glee just  seeing those guys fall though oh my god  things like this both galvanized  community as well as create intrigue  outside of the playerbase it makes for  fun stories to tell I was there during  the rocket launch I'm at the agent in  the desert  I saw the llama in London's Covent  Garden it would be easy for epoch to sit  on their laurels happy that their game  is doing so exceptionally well but they  keep finding new and interesting ways to  not only excite that current player base  but intrigue a much wider audience and  that is something I would love to see  more I'd like to thank both a four-night  battery our subreddit the game  detectives wiki who did such a good job  at investigating each tidbit of  information as well as all the curious  and inquisitive for my fans who took  pictures visited locations and shot  videos your enthusiasm was infectious  and what really made this Arg great I  hope you enjoyed this video about what I  thought was a rather fascinating event  for the community but for more  four-night content make sure you stay  tuned to GameSpot  [Music]

